    {
      "id": 18039,
      "name": "Lemon Chicken Orzo Soup",
      "notes": "Imported from https://www.themediterraneandish.com/lemon-chicken-orzo-soup/",
      "instructions": "1. Soften the vegetables. Heat the olive oil in a large Dutch oven or heavy cooking pot over medium-high heat. When the oil shimmers, add the onion, celery, carrots, and garlic. Season with a good pinch of salt and black pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables have softened, about 5 minutes.\n2. Poach the chicken. Add the chicken, chicken stock, and water. Season with the oregano, turmeric, red pepper flakes, and another pinch of salt and black pepper. Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat to medium-low. Simmer until the chicken is nearly cooked through, 10 to 15 minutes; it will finish cooking after being shredded and returned to the soup. Skim off any foam that rises to the surface.\n3. Add the orzo and peas. Transfer the chicken to a rimmed plate. Add the orzo and frozen peas to the pot. Raise the heat to bring the liquid back to a boil.\n4. Shred the chicken and finish cooking. While the liquid returns to a boil, use two forks to shred the chicken into smaller pieces. Return it to the pot and cook until the orzo is tender with a slight bite, about 8 minutes longer. Make sure the chicken is fully cooked and reaches 165\u00b0F before serving.\n5. Finish and serve. Turn off the heat and stir in the lemon juice and zest, green onions, and parsley. Ladle into bowls and serve.",
